  message: "Independently reproduced by four blinded readability-panel judges on 2026-11-04 (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/readability_panel_11042026/judges/): sample_C judges 1-3 found normalize's 14 edges all on lines 68-85 and 184-193 (every elif arm after the first dropped; rewriting every elif as else-if gives ~219 edges over 14 variables, walk_to_end 7 -> 17), and sample_B judge 1 found the same loss on an if/elif/return chain followed by a statement (format_address 12 edges, true count 14; six-line repro: if x.a: return / elif x.b: return / return x loses the final use). Judge C1 traced it to cfg.py's single alternative read, the same root cause as filed. Two of them also found a SEPARATE over-count: late_capture_edges emits duplicate (variable, def_line, use_line) triples at a nested def's line (_lazy_re_compile reports 10 edges, 7 unique), so 'under-counts, never over' is false for the raw edge list; not this item, noted for the script's dedup."  # bde7
