  clock: 5  # 8fd0
  nonce: 8fd0  # 8fd0
  message: "SATISFIED on the filed instance (the Python if/elif/else chain). Fix merged in PR #2053 (dev fba763f432, rebase-merged 2026-11-05; tree 1119eff00f): cfg_nodes/python.yaml gains an elif_clause conditional, CfgBuilder._process_conditional resolves every alternative with _find_children and _process_alternatives chains them (each elif a condition block whose false edge is the rest of the list); the five nesting grammars resolve one alternative and are pinned (go, typescript, rust). Tests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_cfg.py::TestIfElifChain, red before (4 failed) and green after. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the item's own repro re-run on the merged tree (kakav_fix_11042026/repro_merged_1119eff00f.txt, probe_function.py over elif_repro.py): plain_chain uncovered [] (was {6,7,9}), 8 edges over ch/out across 9 blocks; chain_with_raise uncovered [], 7 edges; chain_in_while_try uncovered [], 17 edges over 3 vars. django regex_helper.normalize (readability panel sample_C): 219 edges, 214 distinct, 14 variables, uncovered [] (was 14 edges over 6 variables with lines 86-182 uncovered). Pre-registered measurements (RESULT.md, before at 603af28925 / after with the fix): self-tree forfeit_refutation core 99 -> 2 of 3115 edged functions, mainstream 150 -> 3 of 1566; DDG edges core 167,947 -> 173,662, mainstream 119,322 -> 150,439; self-claims gate 23 confirmed_with_caveats unchanged (check-self-claims-drift OK); affected-test run 12,644 passed, changed files at 100% coverage. SIBLING SWEEP (required by this item before closing): multiple except_clauses ARE iterated by type (cfg.py _process_try) and match arms ARE iterated over the body container, both probed clean on the merged tree (sibling_repro_merged_1119eff00f.txt: two_excepts and three_cases, except-arm lines all recorded). The try/for/while else_clause is NOT walked (a missing child mapping, a different mechanism): filed as INV-rotol-nobok-huhak-kijaj-tupit-fulub-bohir-pulup with its own repros and census (0.1-1.9% of functions). The general claim that every clause of every Python compound statement is in the CFG is NOT asserted here. NOT measured: the corpus A/B on the io-manifest / bakeoff repos (to be a diff of DDG-edge-producing functions and forfeit sets, never totals). Known unfiled side-finding: late_capture_edges emits duplicate (variable, def_line, use_line) triples at a nested def line (harmless to the walk; score-readability dedupes)."  # 8fd0
